      "user_title": null,
      "bookmarked": false,
      "raw": "<p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 6px; color: rgb(20, 24, 35); font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14px; line-height: 19.32px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">Only allowed Unity to deal damage. Finished with all five heroes in double digits.</p><p style=\"margin: 6px 0px; color: rgb(20, 24, 35); font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14px; line-height: 19.32px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">Biggest risk was getting Lost in the Past. Most of the environment deck was in play, but neutered by Mass Levitation and Mega Computers. Multiple Grappling Hooks to take Lost in the Past out of the play when necessary.</p><p style=\"margin: 6px 0px; color: rgb(20, 24, 35); font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14px; line-height: 19.32px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">Wraith used Infrared Eyepiece to bury Prison Breaks.</p><p style=\"margin: 6px 0px; display: inline; color: rgb(20, 24, 35); font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14px; line-height: 19.32px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">Argent Adept mostly healed himself, gave Unity out-of-turn plays, and allowed Visionary to give Unity out of turn draws.</p><div class=\"text_exposed_show\" style=\"color: rgb(20, 24, 35); font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14px; line-height: 19.32px; display: inline !important; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 6px;\">Legacy boosted damage and used Take Downs and Heroic Interceptions to slow/neuter the villain.</p><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 6px;\">Let the Crooked Cops and Enforcers stay in play and just blasted through the damage reduction and dealt with the card discard.</p></div><p>&nbsp;</p>",
